From 7dda155dcb53bdd8043b75c30dd32d81cace28c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:24:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a setting to hold the link at 8 bits for HDR10
 and HLG on NVIDIA

Some TVs with an 8-bit panel (8 bits with FRC) show more banding with 10 or 12 bits at their
input than with 8. Issue #4 (2026-10-26, a ZBook 17 G6): through its dual-mode port, where
NVIDIA chose 8 bits by itself, HDR10 looked right; through an adapter, at 10 bits, the TV
banded. The user asked to be able to choose 8 bits even where more is possible.

"HDR output depth (NVIDIA)", System > Display, expert level (videoscreen.hadeshdrdepth):
Automatic (the default: "max bpc" is not touched, as before) or 8 bits. With 8 bits, "max bpc"
goes to 8 in every request that signals HDR (the transport of Dolby Vision puts back what it
found, which can be another value) and back to the driver's maximum with the first modeset
after it, so SDR and native Dolby Vision are never held by it; a request made again after a
modeset carries it again (RequeueOutputProperties()). The picture is drawn as before: with the
half-float buffer (videoscreen.hadesfloatoutput) the graphics card brings it down to 8 bits as
it does where the link takes no more, which is the output that the user saw right. Shown only
where the connector has "max bpc" and NV_OUTPUT_BPC (nvidia-drm with the Hades patches), so the
log can say the depth that results: NV_OUTPUT_BPC at 8 bits is then logged as asked for, not
as the driver's own choice. A "max bpc" at 8 found on that output when Kodi takes it (left by a
session that stopped in the middle of an HDR video: nothing else in Kodi sets it to 8 outside
native Dolby Vision, whose leftovers are put back already) is put back to the maximum with the
first modeset, said in the log.

Kodi's dithering setting does nothing visible in HDR there, as the user saw: its automatic
depth is the depth of the framebuffer on an HDR display (LinuxRendererGLES), 16 bits with the
half-float one. That is unchanged.

The decision is KODI::WINDOWING::GBM::HDRDepthFor(), tested on the host (a sequence of the
requests of SetHDR()). Strings in English, translated in Estuary (es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
